 - **Groups in use**: `"player"` (added by `player.gd` in its own `_ready()`, not baked into `player.tscn`, so a node whose `_ready()` runs earlier in the level tree finds nothing: look it up again later, as `WaterManager` does every physics frame while its reference is null), `"trap"`, `"ground"`, `"catwalk"` (a body, or a whole catwalk `TileMapLayer` kept apart from the ground layer: the player's hang probes, the ladder landing and the laser accept anything in it as a catwalk, and water passes it because it is not `"world_tilemap"`; a `PoweredCatwalkLayer` is in it only while out), `"world_tilemap"` (the walkable ground `TileMapLayer`), `"ladder_tilemap"` (every ladder layer: the level's static one and any `PoweredLadderLayer` while it is out; the player reads them all), `"water_manager"` (each level's `WaterManager` instance, looked up by basins/faucets/the player), `"water_solid"` (non-tilemap bodies water particles collide with and can be carried by — moving platform, drop platform, crusher's `ArmBody`, cannon's `StaticBody2D`, laser turret's and arc turret's `Body`, the laser receiver, the bullet target, the see-saw, the breakable barrier, ice blocks while intact), `"laser_mirror"` (every `Mirror`, and a see-saw with `mirror_surface` on; what `LaserBeam` iterates to find reflectors), `"power_target"` (every `PowerTarget`; how a conductor layer finds devices at its terminals), `"power_source"` (every button, speed trap, laser receiver, arc receiver, bullet target, weight plate, angle sensor, basin sensor and zone sensor), `"gem"` (every gem; the player counts the level's total from it at load), `"swing"` (every `Swing`; what the player's grab looks up), `"grab_rail"` (a `Path2D` the player can hang from: a `Rail` node joins it at run time, as does a rail bot's rail; a plain Path2D with no bot is added by hand), `"rail_bot"` (every rail bot; the player's rail hang treats it as an obstacle), `"saveable"` (every node that takes part in checkpoint snapshots — see C